AIM
To develop an AJAX-based web application that retrieves data from a server asynchronously without reloading the entire webpage.

PROCEDURE:


 AJAX – Asynchronous Data Retrieval
1. Create an HTML webpage with a Load Data button.
2. Create an XMLHttpRequest object in JavaScript.
3. Send an asynchronous GET request to the server.
4. Receive and parse the JSON response.
5. Display the received data without refreshing the webpage.
6. Save as 4.html and run it with internet access.

PROGRAM
Save the following code as 4.html. Open it in a browser with internet access and click the Load Data button.

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>AJAX Web Application</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f2f2f2;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 40px;
        }
        .container {
            width: 400px;
            margin: auto;
            padding: 25px;
            background-color: white;
            border-radius: 10px;
        }
        button {
            padding: 12px 20px;
            background-color: #333;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
        #result {
            margin-top: 20px;
            padding: 15px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <h1>AJAX Web Application</h1>
        <button onclick="loadData()">Load Data</button>
        <div id="result">Click the button to load data.</div>
    </div>

    <script>
        function loadData() {
            // Create XMLHttpRequest object
            let xhr = new XMLHttpRequest();

            // Open asynchronous GET request
            xhr.open("GET", "https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts/1", true);

            // Handle server response
            xhr.onload = function() {
                if (xhr.status === 200) {
                    let data = JSON.parse(xhr.responseText);

                    document.getElementById("result").innerHTML =
                        "<h3>" + data.title + "</h3>" +
                        "<p>" + data.body + "</p>";
                }
                else {
                    document.getElementById("result").textContent = "Error loading data.";
                }
            };

            // Handle network error
            xhr.onerror = function() {
                document.getElementById("result").textContent = "Network error occurred.";
            };

            // Send request
            xhr.send();
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>

OUTPUT
Initially, the page displays “Click the button to load data.”
After clicking Load Data, the server response (post title and body) is displayed on the same page without refreshing it.

RESULT
Thus, an AJAX-based web application was successfully developed to retrieve server data asynchronously and display it without reloading the webpage.
